WEBVTT

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:01.301
Hi, my name's Selina.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:05.038
I'm a third year studying Electrical
and Computer Engineering at Carnegie Mellon University.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:09.876
And one of my fun experiences at Carnegie
Mellon involves using the CMU Arts Pass.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:14.114
So all students have something called the
CMU Arts Pass that allows us to attend

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:18.718
museums, exhibitions, and just
events around Pittsburgh for free.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:21.454
So one example is the National Aviary.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:25.091
So the National Aviary is located in Pittsburgh

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:29.295
and it's one of the only independent
indoor nonprofit aviaries in the United States.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:33.767
And it's really large and there's a lot
of birds featured there such as

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:37.804
we saw bald eagles,
peacocks, toucans, penguins.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:42.409
And in this aviary, you're actually allowed
to walk through the bird's natural habitat.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:45.678
So some birds are obviously held in cages.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:50.116
There's a glass door behind you and
this bird, but for other exhibitions,

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.785
you can actually walk through that habitat

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:54.387
and you can actually get
really up close to the birds.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:57.891
So this was a really fun experience
and I think without the CMU Arts Pass,

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.827
it would be kind
of pricey for us to go through.

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:03.696
And also when you're going to all
these events around Pittsburgh,

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.634
you can use your CMU ID as a bus pass.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.002
So my friends and I,

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:11.304
we made a trip out of the National Aviary

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:14.207
and then we followed it
by going to the Mattress Factory.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.809
So actually contrary to its name,

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.377
it's not actually a mattress factory,

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:22.615
but it's rather a contemporary art museum
and it focuses on site-specific installation art.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:26.019
And one thing I found is that Pittsburgh
is actually a very artsy city.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:30.056
We have a lot of famous artists that
came from the city such as Andy Warhol,

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:33.359
and you can see his works exhibited
in almost any museum.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:37.630
So I just think, especially as an Electrical
and Computer Engineering major,

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:42.869
it's great for me and my friends to
be able to explore the arts around Pittsburgh

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.838
and just get a change
of scenery and a change of pace.